<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section" style="padding-bottom:0;"><div style="margin-bottom:44px;"><div class="why-grid"><div class="why-cell why-order-1"><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;border-radius:var(--radius-panel);padding:32px 30px;background:linear-gradient(152deg,#155F9B 0%,#0E4A7C 46%,#0A3860 100%);border:none;"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;margin-bottom:18px;"><img src="~/images/hana-mark-white.svg" alt="" style="width:36px;height:36px;display:block;flex:none;"><span style="flex:1;height:1px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.24);"></span></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:23px;font-weight:600;color:#fff;line-height:1.22;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 12px;text-wrap:balance;">More functionality within a smaller board area</h3><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:14.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.84);line-height:1.6;margin:0 0 16px;">Integrating die, passives and interconnect into one package can reduce the board area occupied by separate components, shorten signal paths and reduce the number of placements required during board assembly.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">Decades of SIP manufacturing experience</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">Shorter interconnect paths for RF and high-speed performance</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">Fewer placements at board assembly</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">Wire bond, flip chip and SMT within one group</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">DFM review before NPI</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">Customer IP protected under ISO 27001</span></li></ul></div></div><div class="why-cell why-photo-cell why-order-2"><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;border-radius:var(--radius-panel);border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--surface);width:100%;height:100%;min-height:320px;"><img src="~/images/sip-why.webp" alt="SiP module with stacked die and passives" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;"></div></